===Etymology===
Alteration (''-ch'' due to {{m|de|Lurch}}) of {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|mol}}, {{m|gmh|molle}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|mol}}, {{m|goh|mollo|mol(l)o}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*mulô}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*molh₂-o-}} (compare Lithuanian {{m|lt|mulvas|mul̃vas}} ‘yellow, clayey’, Latin {{m|la|mulleus}} ‘ruddy (shoes)’, Sanskrit {{term|mála}} ‘dirt’), from {{m|ine-pro|*melh₂-}} ‘dark color’.<ref>Wolfgang Pfeifer, ed., ''Etymologisches Wörterbuch des Deutschen'', s.v. “Molch” (Munich: Deutscher Taschenbucher Vertrag, 2005).</ref> More at {{l|de|malen}}.

